  "id": "Compound::DB01200 - Gene::151",
  "verbalization": "Bromocriptine is linked to Adra2b through a complex network of interactions involving alpha-adrenergic receptor activity and organonitrogen compounds. The evidence suggests that Bromocriptine binds to Adra1b, which in turn participates in alpha-adrenergic receptor activity, and this activity is associated with Adra2b. Additionally, Bromocriptine causes Erythromelalgia, which is linked to Lisuride, a compound that binds to Adra2b. This indicates that Bromocriptine may influence Adra2b through a chain of interactions involving organonitrogen compounds and alpha-adrenergic signaling. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Bromocriptine could modulate Adra2b activity, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
